From cffe176b047ee48d7faa3d57f71dc5f802010630 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:12:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] media: iris: ROG5 diagnostics: firmware SFR, HFI packet
 trace and firmware log

The first k114 trial on the ROG Phone 5 (SM8350, OEM vpu20_4v firmware)
decoded correctly and then hit a firmware fatal error at the end of every
decode session: "sys error (type: 1, session id:ff, data1:1,
data2:deadbead)", that is HFI_EVENT_SYS_ERROR with HFI_ERR_SYS_FATAL and a
firmware-private marker. The log cannot tell which command the firmware
failed on, and the gen1 driver never prints the Subsystem Failure Reason
the firmware writes into the SFR buffer (the stock msm_vidc driver does,
hfi_common.c:2606).

- Keep a ring of the first 32 bytes of the last 64 HFI packets in both
  directions (sent under core->lock in iris_hfi_queue_cmd_write_locked(),
  received in iris_hfi_queue_msg_read()).
- Send the HFI debug config after SYS_INIT, like stock: module parameter
  fw_debug, default 0x18 (error and fatal messages, the stock default
  FW_ERROR | FW_FATAL), queue mode; 0 sends nothing. Firmware debug-queue
  messages are printed (rate limited) and kept in a ring of 16 lines; the
  debug queue is also read after a system error while the queues exist.
- iris_core_dump_diag_locked() prints the SFR text (bounded, sanitised),
  the packet trace and the firmware log. It runs after a system error
  (once the debug queue is drained), before tearing down a failed core
  init (patch 0154) and, rate limited, on fatal session errors.

ROG5: patch 0157, kernel k115. Not in upstream.
